It appearing that in paying tax for the year 1896, according to tax receipt No. 1853, W. X. Reese paid on valuation of $4,000 when it should have been on a valuation of $4,000 the AS being the page number where said assessments appear on the land roll, and that he is entitled to a refund of the difference in these valuations; the Clerk of this Board is therefore directed to issue warrants to W. X. Reese.

Dorothy McBee, Superintendent of Education has this day filed her report.

It appearing that before the next regular meeting of this Board certain bonds and coupons will become due and payable, and that it is necessary that same be paid when due and presented for payment; the Clerk of this Board is therefore directed to issue warrants out of the proper fund.

